
## Q1a: focus on <h2 tabindex=-1> (idx -1, inside)
Tab       prevented=true -> first-btn
Shift+Tab prevented=true -> last-btn

## Q1b: focus on a <summary> in the middle of the list
Tab       prevented=false (browser owns; next is summary2)
Tab@last  prevented=true -> close
Shift+Tab prevented=false (browser owns; prev is close)

## Q1c: focus on a DISABLED control inside (became disabled while focused)
Tab       prevented=true -> first-btn (contained; goes to FIRST, not next)
Shift+Tab prevented=true -> last-btn (contained; goes to LAST, not prev)

## Q1d: focus on a non-heading tabindex=-1 element inside (roving treeitem div)
Tab       prevented=true -> first-btn (contained; jumps to FIRST instead of last-btn)
Shift+Tab prevented=true -> last-btn (contained; jumps to LAST instead of first-btn)

## Q1e: focus OUTSIDE the dialog (body / background control)
body  Tab       prevented=true -> first-btn
body  Shift+Tab prevented=true -> last-btn
bgbtn Tab       prevented=true -> first-btn
null  Tab       prevented=true -> first-btn

## Q1f: dialog with ZERO focusable elements
Tab       prevented=false  <-- false means the browser walks OUT
Shift+Tab prevented=false  <-- false means the browser walks OUT

## Q1g: dialog with exactly ONE focusable
h2   Tab       prevented=true -> only
only Tab       prevented=true -> only
only Shift+Tab prevented=true -> only

## Q1h: ObjectTreeModal — pane <summary role=treeitem> roved to tabindex=-1, focus on the roved series div
open: Tab from h2 prevented=true -> pane1-summary
after ArrowDown: pane1-summary tabindex=-1, series-node tabindex=0
Shift+Tab from series-node prevented=false -> series-node
  browser sequential-backward from series-node skips pane1-summary (tabindex=-1) and h2 (-1): NOTHING inside precedes it -> focus leaves the dialog

## Q1i: Toolbar alertdialog is position:fixed -> offsetParent null in Chromium
Tab       prevented=false  <-- false: dialogs[] is empty after the offsetParent filter
Shift+Tab prevented=false
control (offsetParent non-null): Shift+Tab prevented=true -> switchWarnTitle

## Q2a: STACKED — Help (DOM 105) opened over Settings (DOM 113): selector picks dialogs[last] = Settings
Help h2:      Tab       prevented=true -> settings-search
Help h2:      Shift+Tab prevented=true -> settings-close
Help summary: Tab       prevented=true -> settings-search
Help close:   Tab       prevented=true -> settings-search

## Q2b: STACKED — ThemeEditor (DOM 148) opened over Settings (DOM 113): top is later in DOM
Theme h2:    Shift+Tab prevented=true -> theme-close
Theme close: Tab       prevented=true -> theme-first
Theme first: Shift+Tab prevented=true -> theme-close

## Q2c: context menu only (role=menu) with _openModalCount>0
Tab       prevented=false  (menu is not in the dialog-family selector)

## Scroll-key release scoping
ArrowDown on button in modal:  prevented=false calls=0
Shift+ArrowDown on button:     prevented=false calls=0
Ctrl+ArrowDown on button:      prevented=true calls=1
ArrowDown on listbox option:   prevented=true calls=2
ArrowDown on radio in group:   prevented=false (form-control gate returns first)
ArrowDown on combobox input:   prevented=false
no modal, ArrowDown on button: prevented=true calls=1
